{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b53", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Oscillations - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a929d"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a929a", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9233", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b64c478ae845c43c6818"], "question": {"text": "Two simple harmonic motions are represented by the equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math> The amplitude of the second motion is _____ times the amplitude in the first motion."}, "options": [{"id": "c961b4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9234"}, {"id": "ee5a65", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9235"}, {"id": "f29203", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9236"}, {"id": "090ac2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9237"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9238", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "<p>A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is attached with two identical springs of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> each. The block is placed on a frictionless surface and the ends of the springs are attached to rigid supports (see figure). When the mass is displaced from its equilibrium position, it executes a simple harmonic motion. The time period of oscillation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mi>X</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math> in SI unit. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> is______.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe0e3bded-73df-40f4-8f4d-8706cf92312e-9893856.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 269px; height: 62px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b53a4d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9239"}, {"id": "54afc1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923a"}, {"id": "e68aba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923b"}, {"id": "fb9594", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b53"], "question": {"text": "When the displacement of a simple harmonic oscillator is one third of its amplitude, the ratio of total energy to the kinetic energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_________."}, "options": [{"id": "3b96ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923e"}, {"id": "036cfa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a923f"}, {"id": "2b3c2d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9240"}, {"id": "c15083", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9241"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9242", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "<p>The time period of simple harmonic motion of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> in the given figure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>, where the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> is _______.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8f9fea0d-8511-4e9b-8b50-7bf9780073e0.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 250px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "c08cba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9243"}, {"id": "0ed1c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9244"}, {"id": "be7618", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9245"}, {"id": "53e638", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9246"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9247", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c6314"], "question": {"text": "Two waves executing simple harmonic motion travelling in the same direction with same amplitude and frequency are superimposed. The resultant amplitude is equal to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> times of amplitude of individual motions. The phase difference between the two motions is _____ (degree)"}, "options": [{"id": "f3949b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9248"}, {"id": "454a49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9249"}, {"id": "49dad4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924a"}, {"id": "67769d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c631c"], "question": {"text": "<p>A simple pendulum with length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and bob of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is executing S.H.M of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The maximum tension in the string is found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4b65b4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924d"}, {"id": "04c3e2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924e"}, {"id": "9252e0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a924f"}, {"id": "4c0e99", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9250"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9251", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8f87"], "question": {"text": "A mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, attached to a horizontal spring, executes SHM with an amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When this mass passes through its mean position, then a smaller mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>124</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is placed over it and both masses move together with amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "84286f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9252"}, {"id": "1d791c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9253"}, {"id": "392715", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9254"}, {"id": "3f8fab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9255"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9256", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d33"], "question": {"text": "A mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is suspended from a spring of negligible mass and the system oscillates with a frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The frequency of oscillations if a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>m</mi></math> is suspended from the same spring is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "e67e26", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9257"}, {"id": "f9f12b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9258"}, {"id": "67096c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9259"}, {"id": "7d3457", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two simple harmonic motion, are represented by the equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Ratio of amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "466fab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925c"}, {"id": "3431e5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925d"}, {"id": "7a6cc7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925e"}, {"id": "53cdd8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a925f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9260", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "The general displacement of a simple harmonic oscillator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> be its time period. The slope of its potential energy (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi></math>) &ndash; time (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>) curve will be maximum when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "190213", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9261"}, {"id": "705248", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9262"}, {"id": "375fbc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9263"}, {"id": "d046df", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9264"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9265", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "<p>As per given figures, two springs of spring constants <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> are connected to mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the period of oscillation in figure (a) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, then the period of oscillation in figure (b) will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F31b05ae5-a3c7-4f0a-a3a7-ac2bdd21af50-1.jpg?alt=media\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 283px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8e49a2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9266"}, {"id": "ff4f6a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9267"}, {"id": "9ccdb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9268"}, {"id": "d72d88", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9269"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c631c"], "question": {"text": "A pendulum bob has a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;at its lowest position. The pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> long. The speed of bob, when the length makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> to the vertical will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "1a5a3d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926b"}, {"id": "24cede", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926c"}, {"id": "ebc262", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926d"}, {"id": "9b8384", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a926f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b64c478ae845c43c6818"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion with an amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. At the mean position, velocity of the particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The distance of the particle from the mean position when its speed becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo></math>______."}, "options": [{"id": "36a57c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9270"}, {"id": "441dd8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9271"}, {"id": "8d757d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9272"}, {"id": "55ac13", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9273"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9274", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "A rectangular block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> attached to a horizontal spiral spring executes simple harmonic motion of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The maximum force exerted by spring on block is ___ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "d0564f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9275"}, {"id": "8d03cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9276"}, {"id": "a005b3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9277"}, {"id": "6a516b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9278"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9279", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8f87"], "question": {"text": "The amplitude of a particle executing SHM is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The displacement at which its kinetic energy will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> more than the potential energy is: ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "4ffdd6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927a"}, {"id": "19509a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927b"}, {"id": "cfb6ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927c"}, {"id": "cddb46", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass $0.50 \\mathrm{~kg}$ executes simple harmonic motion under force $F=-50\\left(\\mathrm{Nm}^{-1}\\right) x$. The time period of oscillation is $\\frac{x}{35} \\mathrm{~s}$. The value of $x$ is _______\n(Given $\\pi=\\frac{22}{7}$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "2c8279", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a927f"}, {"id": "701247", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9280"}, {"id": "6c4688", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9281"}, {"id": "59c896", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9282"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9283", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "A particle performs simple harmonic motion with a period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> second. The time taken by the particle to cover a displacement equal to half of its amplitude from the mean position is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> to the nearest integer is"}, "options": [{"id": "2e446a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9284"}, {"id": "b1aca7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9285"}, {"id": "ee913f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9286"}, {"id": "470c37", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9287"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9288", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c631c"], "question": {"text": "Time period of a simple pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. The time taken to complete <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> oscillations starting from mean position is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mi>T</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "ecc9c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9289"}, {"id": "336efc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928a"}, {"id": "67dcf3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928b"}, {"id": "1ff538", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "<p>The velocity of a particle executing SHM varies with displacement (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>) as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The time period of oscillations is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.</p><p>[Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "15dae3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928e"}, {"id": "e93c4f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a928f"}, {"id": "52c5f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9290"}, {"id": "5bfcd9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9291"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9292", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion. Its amplitude is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and time period is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The time it will take to travel from its position of maximum displacement to the point corresponding to half of its amplitude, is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "4efd42", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9293"}, {"id": "cf1dc4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9294"}, {"id": "d25567", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9295"}, {"id": "5aa44f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9296"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:53.153Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:53.153Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a929c"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:13:30.541Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:01.893Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 20, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e8d9cbf3c651304afb4", "testId": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b53", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:06:21.929Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 40, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a929a", "questions": [{"questionId": "69de4f9d2ee0e063d92a9233", "markedOptions": [], "inputValue": null, "timeTaken": 0, "timeLeftWhenAttempted": null, "status": "notVisited", 